        {1\text{/}\sqrt{2}} & {- 1\text{/}\sqrt{2}} \\
        {1\text{/}\sqrt{2}} & {1\text{/}\sqrt{2}}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Then $P$ orthogonally diagonalizes $A$, so the change of variable $\textbf{x} = P\textbf{y}$ produces the quadratic form $\textbf{y}^{T}D\textbf{y} = 3y_{1}^{2} + 7y_{2}^{2}$. The new axes for this change of variable are shown in Figure 3(a).

