exercise_group.instructions:
Find an SVD of each matrix in Exercises 5–12. [Hint:In Exercise 11, one choice for $U$ is] $\begin{bmatrix}
        {- 1\text{/}3} & {2\text{/}3} & {2\text{/}3} \\
        {2\text{/}3} & {- 1\text{/}3} & {2\text{/}3} \\
        {2\text{/}3} & {2\text{/}3} & {- 1\text{/}3}
        \end{bmatrix}\,.$ In Exercise 12, one column of $U$ can be $\left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
        {1\text{/}\sqrt{6}} \\
        {- 2\text{/}\sqrt{6}} \\
        {1\text{/}\sqrt{6}}
        \end{array} \right\rbrack\,$.﻿

